WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.125
Welcome to the Reliable Agent Capstone.
Your goal is not

2
00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:08.250
to build the largest or most autonomous
agent. Your goal

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.375
is to prove that one useful workflow can
be understood,

4
00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:16.500
bounded, tested, observed, recovered,
revised, and handed to another operator

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.625
with evidence they can independently
review. This is a fictional,

6
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:24.750
offline learning exercise. Nothing in the
lab sends a message,

7
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.875
calls a model, contacts a provider, or
creates a real

8
00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:33.000
approval.

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.381
Begin with a bounded mission whose effects
can be simulated

10
00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:41.762
or safely reversed. Define the user,
desired outcome, inputs, non-goals,

11
00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:46.143
acceptance criteria, stop conditions, and
residual risks. Reliability is not

12
00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:50.524
the same as task size. Write the state
transitions before

13
00:00:50.524 --> 00:00:54.905
selecting a model or provider. At minimum,
distinguish intake, planning,

14
00:00:54.905 --> 00:00:59.286
authorization, execution, verification,
reconciliation, completion, and failure.

15
00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:03.667
For each transition, name the durable
record that proves it

16
00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:08.048
occurred. Follow one synthetic support
case through that diagram. At

17
00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:12.429
intake, record its case identifier and
immutable input hash. Planning

18
00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:16.810
may propose a response, but authorization
must create a separate

19
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.190
approval record. Execution uses a durable
operation key. Verification reads

20
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:25.571
the simulated destination. Reconciliation
decides whether an uncertain write

21
00:01:25.571 --> 00:01:29.952
occurred. Completion is allowed only when
the observed postcondition matches

22
00:01:29.952 --> 00:01:34.333
the authorized case and operation key.
Keep portable responsibilities separate

23
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:38.714
from provider adapters. Anthropic, OpenAI,
and Google examples may differ

24
00:01:38.714 --> 00:01:43.095
in tools or tracing syntax, but no adapter
may silently

25
00:01:43.095 --> 00:01:47.476
redefine authority or the evidence
contract. Meta Llama, Qwen, DeepSeek,

26
00:01:47.476 --> 00:01:51.857
Mistral, and Microsoft Phi identify model
families or projects. A

27
00:01:51.857 --> 00:01:56.238
local runtime, hosted service, and agent
framework are different operational

28
00:01:56.238 --> 00:02:00.619
contracts. Validate each adapter instead
of assuming shared tool calling,

29
00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:05.000
authorization, telemetry, or
structured-output behavior.

30
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.333
Checkpoint. Before automation, can a
reviewer identify every allowed

31
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:13.667
transition, the durable evidence for each
transition, the stop conditions,

32
00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:18.000
and the system that alone may authorize an
effect?

33
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.750
A workflow is not ready to automate if any

34
00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.500
transition, evidence record, stop
condition, or authority owner is unclear.

35
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.250
Narrow the mission and make the missing
contract explicit before

36
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.000
choosing a model.

37
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.111
Inventory every model, tool, data source,
credential, human role, and

38
00:03:37.111 --> 00:03:41.222
destination. For each tool, record its
allowed operation, denied operations,

39
00:03:41.222 --> 00:03:45.333
input validation, approval requirement,
execution limit, postcondition, audit

40
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:49.444
event, and recovery behavior. Draw trust
boundaries around untrusted user

41
00:03:49.444 --> 00:03:53.556
input, retrieved content, model output,
MCP servers, secret-bearing executors,

42
00:03:53.556 --> 00:03:57.667
memory, and external systems. Instructions
inside data remain data until

43
00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:01.778
a trusted control plane validates them.
Threat-model prompt injection,

44
00:04:01.778 --> 00:04:05.889
confused-deputy behavior, excessive
permission, secret exposure, replay,

45
00:04:05.889 --> 00:04:10.000
duplicate writes, poisoned memory, unsafe
delegation, and misleading success claims.

46
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.111
Each material threat needs prevention,
detection, containment, and recovery. A

47
00:04:14.111 --> 00:04:18.222
model may propose an action, but
confidence never grants authority.

48
00:04:18.222 --> 00:04:22.333
The trusted executor performs
deterministic identity, policy, approval,

49
00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:26.444
limit, audit, and postcondition checks. In
this lab, ticket text

50
00:04:26.444 --> 00:04:30.556
is deterministic fixture data and the
destination is a local

51
00:04:30.556 --> 00:04:34.667
directory. No model runs and no message is
sent. Passing

52
00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.778
fixture tests does not qualify
authentication, provider behavior, rate

53
00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:42.889
limits, network failure handling, data
handling, or reconciliation in a

54
00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:47.000
live destination.

55
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.500
Checkpoint. Model confidence never grants
authority. Why is a deny-all

56
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.000
policy also an invalid repair?

57
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Deny-all is not a repair because it hides
whether the

58
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.000
validator compares evidence correctly. A
valid revised package and an

59
00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.000
independently changed valid case must
pass. The correct control rejects

60
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:55.000
stale or mismatched bindings while
accepting packages whose values match

61
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.000
the manifest.

62
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.313
For each step, define the minimum context
packet: objective, constraints,

63
00:06:03.313 --> 00:06:07.625
authoritative evidence, current state,
tool contract, output schema, and

64
00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:11.938
escalation rule. Exclude stale,
irrelevant, unrelated, and secret

65
00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:16.250
material. Separate working context from
durable memory. State what may

66
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:20.563
be remembered, who may read it, how it
expires, how

67
00:06:20.563 --> 00:06:24.875
corrections propagate, and which source
wins when memory conflicts with

68
00:06:24.875 --> 00:06:29.188
current evidence. For MCP or multi-agent
work, document capability discovery,

69
00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:33.500
identity, authorization, input and output
validation, delegation limits, timeouts,

70
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.813
idempotency, and handoff acceptance. A
receiving component must reject an

71
00:06:37.813 --> 00:06:42.125
incomplete handoff without guessing. The
package binding is a concrete

72
00:06:42.125 --> 00:06:46.438
contract. The attempt identifier says
which submission is under review.

73
00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:50.750
The version identifies its revision. The
case identifier identifies the

74
00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.063
evaluated input. The outcome identifies
the observed result. If a

75
00:06:55.063 --> 00:06:59.375
referenced artifact belongs to another
attempt, version, case, or outcome,

76
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:03.688
the receiver must reject it even when the
file exists.

77
00:07:03.688 --> 00:07:08.000
Filenames establish location, not
provenance.

78
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.500
Checkpoint. Is a handoff a conversational
promise, a directory-existence check,

79
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.000
or a contract with evidence?

80
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.250
A handoff is a contract with evidence. The
receiver must

81
00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.500
be able to compare the packet with the
manifest, reject

82
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.750
stale or incomplete material, and identify
what remains unresolved. Existing

83
00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:17.000
filenames do not establish that
relationship.

84
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:21.188
Build a representative evaluation set with
routine cases, boundary cases,

85
00:08:21.188 --> 00:08:25.375
adversarial inputs, and known failure
modes. Use deterministic checks where

86
00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:29.563
possible and calibrated human review where
judgment is necessary. Test

87
00:08:29.563 --> 00:08:33.750
tool denial, malformed output, timeouts,
partial writes, duplicate requests, stale

88
00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.938
context, poisoned instructions, provider
unavailability, and missing telemetry.

89
00:08:37.938 --> 00:08:42.125
Record expected containment before
execution and the observed result

90
00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:46.313
afterward. Do not retry an uncertain
external action until the

91
00:08:46.313 --> 00:08:50.500
destination is reconciled. A retry must be
idempotent or protected

92
00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.688
by a durable operation key, and recovery
evidence must show

93
00:08:54.688 --> 00:08:58.875
that it did not duplicate or conceal an
effect. The

94
00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:03.063
lab adds deterministic checks for exact
criterion identifiers, integer score

95
00:09:03.063 --> 00:09:07.250
ranges, total arithmetic,
evidence-reference syntax, file existence,

96
00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:11.438
and binding to attempt, version, case, and
outcome. Those checks

97
00:09:11.438 --> 00:09:15.625
establish structural consistency only.
They do not decide whether prose

98
00:09:15.625 --> 00:09:19.813
is safe, useful, or truthful, and they do
not qualify

99
00:09:19.813 --> 00:09:24.000
a live integration.

100
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.000
Checkpoint. A happy-path demonstration
proves possibility. What does a failure

101
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
test add?

102
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.250
A failure test supplies evidence of
control. It can show

103
00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:23.500
detection, containment, reconciliation,
safe retry, or recovery. A changed-input

104
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.750
test also helps reveal a hard-coded
repair. The expected decision

105
00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:32.000
and the observed evidence must both be
recorded.

106
00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.063
Design privacy-aware observability and the
operating runbook together. Correlate

107
00:10:36.063 --> 00:10:40.125
workflow, agent, model, tool, handoff,
approval, and outcome events. Record

108
00:10:40.125 --> 00:10:44.188
versions, latency, error class, state
transitions, evaluation results, and

109
00:10:44.188 --> 00:10:48.250
secure evidence references. Redact
prompts, secrets, personal data, sensitive

110
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:52.313
tool payloads, and hidden reasoning.
Define indicators that reveal user

111
00:10:52.313 --> 00:10:56.375
harm or control failure, not only
infrastructure health. Include evaluation

112
00:10:56.375 --> 00:11:00.438
regressions, policy denials, incomplete
traces, duplicate-effect attempts,

113
00:11:00.438 --> 00:11:04.500
unresolved reconciliations, and
evidence-integrity failures. The synthetic

114
00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:08.563
lab trace is intentionally small:
validator version, package path, decision

115
00:11:08.563 --> 00:11:12.625
code, score, and pass status. Do not copy
ticket bodies

116
00:11:12.625 --> 00:11:16.688
or fictional approvals into telemetry. The
operating runbook covers detection,

117
00:11:16.688 --> 00:11:20.750
triage, containment, reconciliation, safe
retry, rollback, escalation,

118
00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:24.813
communication, recovery verification, and
post-incident improvement. Name the owner

119
00:11:24.813 --> 00:11:28.875
and evidence required at each decision
point. Incident response is

120
00:11:28.875 --> 00:11:32.938
broader than this validator, so do not
present the lab

121
00:11:32.938 --> 00:11:37.000
as a live incident qualification.

122
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.000
Checkpoint. What should useful telemetry
answer, and what must it

123
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.000
avoid becoming?

124
00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.800
Useful telemetry answers what happened,
which decision was made, what

125
00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:35.600
evidence supports it, and what action
comes next. It must

126
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.400
not become a second data leak. Redact
sensitive content and

127
00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.200
retain only the operational fields needed
for diagnosis, accountability, and

128
00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:47.000
recovery.

129
00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.500
Submit exactly eight required artifacts:
architecture-and-state-model.md,

130
00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.000
tool-inventory-and-permission-matrix.md,
trust-boundary-and-threat-model.md,

131
00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.500
evaluation-set-and-rubric.json,
failure-tests-and-results.md,

132
00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:01.000
observability-plan.md,
operating-runbook.md, and

133
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:04.500
evidence-map-and-handoff.md. Map every
rubric judgment to a submitted artifact or

134
00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:08.000
assessment result. The six criteria total
100 points: reliable-capstone-correctness

135
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:11.500
is 20, reliable-capstone-safety is 20,
reliable-capstone-evidence is 15,

136
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:15.000
reliable-capstone-reliability is 20,
reliable-capstone-maintainability is 15,

137
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.500
and reliable-capstone-communication is 10.
The pass threshold is 80 percent.

138
00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.000
A score without a traceable evidence
reference is invalid, even

139
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.500
if the conclusion sounds reasonable.
Compare complete and flawed exemplars

140
00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.000
by evidence, not polish. The flawed
package has broad authority,

141
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.500
three easy cases, blind retry, invasive
telemetry, and no actionable

142
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:36.000
handoff. Preserve the failed submission,
feedback, revised artifacts, and final

143
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.500
handoff. Completion requires a passing
knowledge check and a capstone

144
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:43.000
score of at least 80 percent.

145
00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:47.467
Compare two fictional support-triage
packages. The complete package uses

146
00:13:47.467 --> 00:13:51.933
synthetic tickets, explicit states, a
durable case identifier and operation

147
00:13:51.933 --> 00:13:56.400
key, human approval before a sandbox
effect, nine failure tests,

148
00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:00.867
redacted traces, destination read-back,
and an owned runbook. Every score

149
00:14:00.867 --> 00:14:05.333
points to artifacts and test identifiers.
The flawed package says

150
00:14:05.333 --> 00:14:09.800
the agent resolves tickets, grants all
tools, trusts user text,

151
00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:14.267
asks the same evaluator to judge three
easy cases, retries

152
00:14:14.267 --> 00:14:18.733
every timeout, stores sensitive material
forever, and declares success because

153
00:14:18.733 --> 00:14:23.200
the demonstration looked good. Its
polished language cannot replace state,

154
00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:27.667
authority, representative testing, privacy
controls, reconciliation, or evidence. The

155
00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:32.133
complete exemplar scores 20 plus 20 plus
15 plus 20

156
00:14:32.133 --> 00:14:36.600
plus 15 plus 10, which equals 100 points.
The flawed

157
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:41.067
exemplar scores 8 plus 5 plus 5 plus 6

158
00:14:41.067 --> 00:14:45.533
plus 4 plus 3, which equals 31 points.
These are

159
00:14:45.533 --> 00:14:50.000
supplied calibration records, not live
approvals or production decisions.

160
00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:53.750
Choose the weakest criterion in your first
submission. Name the

161
00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:57.500
exact artifact or assessment result that
should support it, the

162
00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:01.250
evidence currently missing, and the
smallest revision that would make

163
00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:05.000
the handoff reviewable.

164
00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:39.000
Checkpoint. A reviewer believes the
workflow is safe but cannot

165
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:43.000
link the safety score to a submitted
artifact or assessment

166
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.000
result. Is the score valid?

167
00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.286
The score is invalid. Reviewer confidence
cannot replace criterion evidence.

168
00:17:51.286 --> 00:17:55.571
Link safety points to the permission
matrix, threat model, containment

169
00:17:55.571 --> 00:17:59.857
test, privacy controls, approval record,
or relevant assessment result. If

170
00:17:59.857 --> 00:18:04.143
the evidence does not exist, lower the
score and revise

171
00:18:04.143 --> 00:18:08.429
the package. One overall screenshot is not
enough. Stable artifact

172
00:18:08.429 --> 00:18:12.714
and test references let another reviewer
reproduce why each point

173
00:18:12.714 --> 00:18:17.000
was awarded without hidden reasoning.

174
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:21.000
Open the reliable-agent capstone. Produce
the eight artifacts, execute routine,

175
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:25.000
adversarial, and recovery tests, define
privacy-aware telemetry and the runbook,

176
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.000
map all six criteria to evidence,
self-score against both exemplars,

177
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.000
preserve feedback, revise failing
evidence, and deliver the operational

178
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:37.000
handoff with residual limits.

179
00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.500
Now repair the evidence-binding defect.
The failed fixture declares attempt-1,

180
00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:46.000
version 1.0.0, case support-017, outcome
failed, and an 80-point score.

181
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.500
Several referenced files actually carry
attempt-0, version 0.9.0, or outcome

182
00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:55.000
passed. The starter validator checks
shared package rules and confirms

183
00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:59.500
that filenames exist, but omits binding
equality. It therefore prints

184
00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:04.000
VALID score=80 pass=true and exits with
code 0. That is

185
00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:08.500
unearned credit because existence proves
location, not provenance. The missing

186
00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:13.000
invariant is equality of each artifact
binding with the manifest's

187
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:17.500
attempt identifier, version, case
identifier, and outcome. The focused

188
00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:22.000
repair reads the first line of each
Markdown artifact, requires

189
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:26.500
the Evidence-Binding prefix, parses its
JSON, and compares those four

190
00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:31.000
values. The evaluation JSON uses its
binding object. The first

191
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.500
mismatch must produce E_BINDING with the
artifact and key. The

192
00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:40.000
repaired validator must still accept
revised, complete, and changed valid

193
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:44.500
packages, so deny-all is not a valid
repair. The revised

194
00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:49.000
fixture uses attempt-2, version 1.1.0,
case support-017, outcome passed. The

195
00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:53.500
changed-input fixture changes case
support-017 to support-099 in the

196
00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:58.000
manifest, every binding, and the synthetic
input text. Acceptance proves

197
00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:02.500
comparison of values rather than a
hard-coded case. Exact commands

198
00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:07.000
and outputs are selectable in the visual
artifact. The starter

199
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:11.500
CLI on failed prints VALID score=80
pass=true and exits 0.

200
00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:16.000
Starter tests finish with TESTS total=8
passed=7 failed=1 and exit

201
00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:20.500
1. The reference CLI on failed prints
INVALID E_BINDING

202
00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:25.000
architecture-and-state-model.md:attemptId
and exits 1. The reference CLI on revised

203
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:29.500
prints VALID score=80 pass=true and exits
0. Reference tests finish

204
00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:34.000
with TESTS total=8 passed=8 failed=0 and
exit 0. This is

205
00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:38.500
fixture simulation. No API, model, MCP
server, human approver, external

206
00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:43.000
ticket system, or real write is invoked.
These strings are

207
00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:47.500
teaching records, not signed approvals.
The offline package check does

208
00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:52.000
not evaluate model quality, live safety,
or human judgment.

209
00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:55.750
Before editing, predict the first error
from the failed fixture.

210
00:23:55.750 --> 00:23:59.500
Which artifact and which binding key
should the validator report?

211
00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:03.250
Then explain why checking only that the
file exists would

212
00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:07.000
be insufficient.

213
00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:26.000
The first mismatch is
architecture-and-state-model.md at

214
00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:30.000
attemptId. The file exists, but its
evidence belongs to another

215
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:34.000
attempt. A filename establishes location
only. The validator must compare

216
00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:38.000
attempt identifier, version, case
identifier, and outcome with the manifest,

217
00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:42.000
in that order, and report the first
mismatch.

218
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:46.296
From the repository root, run the starter
CLI against the

219
00:25:46.296 --> 00:25:50.593
failed fixture and record its incorrect
successful decision. Then run

220
